---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="Who I am and how this devlog works.">
  <section class="page prose">
    <div class="chips t-dot"><span class="b">ABOUT</span><span>THE HUMAN IN THE LOOP</span></div>
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      Hi, I'm Mario, from Spain. My day job is Jira administration, and game development is what I'm passionate
      about: I started teaching myself to code many years ago, in C#, while learning Unity.
    </p>
    <p>Right now my goal is to find out the real potential of AI in today's development environments.</p>
    <p>Thanks for visiting my small space on the internet!</p>

    <h2>What I'm doing right now</h2>
    <p>
      Learning by building. Kotomachi Gakuen, the game, is the main project, and around it I'm practising the stuff that real teams
      use: architecture decision records, Jira and Confluence, CI, and reviews that end in a clear READY or NOT READY.
    </p>

    <h2>The crew</h2>
    <p>
      Think of the agents as different workers, each one with their own field. They audit each other, so one of them
      can't greenlight something that isn't properly tested. I call the way we work <em>Ringi</em> (稟議), after the
      Japanese approval process: a proposal goes around collecting everyone's stamp, and mine is always the last one.
    </p>
    <ul class="crewlist">
      <li><span class="t-dot">CLAUDE</span><span>Builds: writes most of the code and the first drafts.</span></li>
      <li><span class="t-dot">CHATGPT</span><span>Reviews: designs, documents and the decisions behind them.</span></li>
      <li><span class="t-dot">CODEX</span><span>Audits the code. Same family as ChatGPT, different job.</span></li>
      <li><span class="t-dot">MARIO</span><span>Decides every point, every merge and every closed ticket.</span></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How this site works</h2>
    <p>
      Built with Astro and hosted on GitHub Pages. Every entry goes through a pull request, and merging it is my
      approval. Drafts are written with help from AI assistants, then reviewed and edited by me. The dioramas are drawn
      in code, one per post.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
